At the time of the 2011 census, 93.00% of the population spoke [[Telugu language|Telugu]] and 6.12% [[Urdu]] as their first language.<ref name="language">{{Cite web |title=Table C-16 Population by Mother Tongue: Andhra Pradesh |url=https://censusindia.gov.in/nada/index.php/catalog/10193/download/13305/DDW-C16-STMT-MDDS-2800.XLSX |website=[[Census of India]] |publisher=[[Registrar General and Census Commissioner of India]]}}</ref> Hinduism is a majority in the district, while Christians are a significant (underreported) minority of around 15-20% in the district. Muslim make up around 7% of the population.

== Administrative divisions ==

The district is divided into  [[Bapatla revenue division|Bapatla]], [[Chirala revenue division|Chirala]] and [[Repalle revenue division|Repalle]], which are further subdivided into a total of 20 [[Tehsil|mandal]]s.<ref name="district-map">{{Cite web |title=Bapatla district map, with mandals and revenue divisions |url=https://bapatla.ap.gov.in/map-of-district/ |access-date=2026-02-21 |website=Bapatla district, Government of Andhra Pradesh}}</ref><ref name="districts-20253112"/><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/vijayawada/andhra-pradesh-gets-76th-revenue-division-bapatlas-repalle-is-headquarters/articleshow/93491442.cms |title=Andhra Pradesh gets 76th revenue division, Bapatla's Repalle |date=2022-08-11 |access-date=2023-05-16 |website=TOI}}</ref>

